<p>
I see a man<br>
sleeping on a bench<br>
in the cold,
</p>

<p>
And I say,
</p>

<p>
&ldquo;Thank you, Lord,<br>
for I am not like him.&rdquo;
</p>

<p>
I see a woman<br>
alone, in tears,<br>
mourning,
</p>

<p>
And I say,
</p>

<p>
&ldquo;Thank you, Lord,<br>
for I am not like her.&rdquo;
</p>

<p>
I see a man<br>
upon a cross,<br>
humiliated, scorned,<br>
despised,
</p>

<p>
And suddenly my<br>
foolish pride is clear<br>
even to me,
</p>

<p>
And I cry,
</p>

<p>
&ldquo;Forgive me, Lord,<br>
for I am not like you.&rdquo;
</p>

<p>
<i>Amen</i>
</p>


